WEBVTT

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:13.106
I wasn't there the day
Dr. Andrew Brown's life changed forever.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.305
But like most folks in Everwood...

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:18.918
...I've heard the story enough times
to be able to tell it.

00:00:19.086 --> 00:00:21.919
It begins where many stories begin...

00:00:22.089 --> 00:00:25.354
...in the city of New York,
where Dr. Brown lived comfortably...

00:00:25.526 --> 00:00:27.324
...with his wife
and two children.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:30.327
- Ephram, you're gonna be late again.
- I know, I know.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.397
Finish your orange juice, sweetie.

00:00:32.566 --> 00:00:34.034
- Good morning.
- This mine?

00:00:34.201 --> 00:00:35.327
It is.

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:38.870
- Someone's unusually quiet this morning.
- Someone's unusually interested.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.736
Don't be nervous about tonight.
Your dad and I'll be there.

00:00:41.909 --> 00:00:44.241
Yeah, I'm sure. See you.

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.971
- His recital's tonight?
- I've only told you 10 times.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.479
- What time?
- Eight. He's going early with a friend.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.414
We're leaving at 7
to make it on time.

00:00:51.585 --> 00:00:54.145
Tell me why, with all the
piano teachers in Manhattan...

00:00:54.321 --> 00:00:56.983
- ...my son has to study in New Jersey?
- The best is in Jersey.

00:00:57.157 --> 00:01:00.525
- I didn't think Jersey had the best anything.
- The Giants play in Jersey.

00:01:00.694 --> 00:01:02.788
- They're not from New Jersey.
- They should be.

00:01:02.963 --> 00:01:04.988
What do you know? You're 8.

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.826
- Bye.
- Be home on time.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.593
I will.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.067
Glioblastoma multiforme.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.972
I call it the great white of brain tumors.
It's malignant and grows quickly.

00:01:17.144 --> 00:01:20.808
Typically occurring in the frontal or
temporal lobe of the cerebral hemisphere.

00:01:20.981 --> 00:01:23.882
In your case, Mr. Saddlebrook,
it occurs in both hemispheres...

00:01:24.051 --> 00:01:26.520
...and has begun to metastasize
into the spinal fluid.

00:01:26.687 --> 00:01:30.021
We know all this already. The other doctors
diagnosed him weeks ago.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.455
They say it's inoperable.
We came to you because you're the best.

00:01:33.627 --> 00:01:38.189
I'm willing to go after this cancer with all
I've got. Starting with radiation therapies...

00:01:38.365 --> 00:01:41.198
...followed by an immediate
and massive surgical resection.

00:01:41.368 --> 00:01:42.961
- Thank you.
- Don't thank me now.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.900
You can thank me
when I save your life.

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:50.741
I hope he's as good as he is brief.

00:01:50.911 --> 00:01:54.211
Night fell and a nasty storm rolled in.

00:01:54.381 --> 00:01:57.214
They don't know the first thing
about this medicine in Boston.

00:01:57.384 --> 00:01:59.375
You asked me to remind you
when it was 7:00.

00:01:59.553 --> 00:02:01.521
- It's 7:00?
- It was 7:00 a half-hour ago...

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:05.124
- ...when I reminded you the first time.
- Tell Julia to go without me.

00:02:05.292 --> 00:02:06.885
She called to say she was leaving.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.086
And she asked me to remind you
that you're a lousy husband/father.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.789
Thanks, Barb.
I don't care!

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:16.425
Look, Larry, listen to me. Listen to me.
The fact remains...

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:21.165
In his usual fashion,
Dr. Brown worked late again.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:25.437
So late, he was still at the hospital
when he received the news.

00:02:31.418 --> 00:02:34.217
Excuse me, ma'am.
We're looking for Dr. Andrew Brown.

00:02:34.388 --> 00:02:36.379
Dr. Brown....

00:02:36.957 --> 00:02:38.891
I'm Andrew Brown.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:44.661
There had been,
it seemed, an accident.

00:02:45.065 --> 00:02:50.629
Sadly, Andy's wife never made it from
home to their son's recital that night.

00:02:50.804 --> 00:02:54.240
Instead, her life was taken tragically...

00:02:54.408 --> 00:02:57.776
...on the icy highway in between.

00:03:38.852 --> 00:03:43.756
Oh, sure, the Browns did the best
they could to get by after that.

00:03:43.924 --> 00:03:46.985
Pretending as though
nothing had changed...

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.130
...knowing that everything had.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:04.643
As expected, Dr. Brown wasted
no time going back to work.

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:09.408
What wasn't expected was
what happened once he got there.

00:04:11.318 --> 00:04:14.413
- Morning, doc.
- Morning, Mr. Saddlebrook.

00:04:14.588 --> 00:04:17.285
- You ready for the big day tomorrow?
- Well, I hope so.

00:04:17.858 --> 00:04:20.190
Say, listen, doc...

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.658
...I heard about the tragedy
you suffered.

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:24.388
I'm sorry.

00:04:31.338 --> 00:04:34.273
If you could be anywhere
in the world right now...

00:04:34.775 --> 00:04:36.004
...where would it be?

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:39.137
Hershey, Pennsylvania.

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:42.346
It's where I was brought up.

00:04:42.516 --> 00:04:44.610
I've kept my parents' farm there.

00:04:45.252 --> 00:04:46.777
Go there.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.546
Now.

00:04:48.989 --> 00:04:50.514
Today.

00:04:52.826 --> 00:04:55.022
I can't save your life.

00:04:55.195 --> 00:04:57.892
At best, I could prolong
it eight months, maybe a year.

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:02.397
Most of that time, you'll be barely
coherent, recovering from surgery.

00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:06.802
And that's all so this hospital can brag
about its statistics with terminal illnesses.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:09.533
But statistics don't measure quality of life.

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:12.508
If you have even the slightest hope
of preserving your own...

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:16.638
...you'll get out of bed and leave this
place as fast as your legs will carry you.

00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:20.048
And those were Andy Brown's
final words...

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:21.984
...as a big city doctor.

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:24.556
- Moving where?!
- Everwood, Colorado.

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:26.556
- Where's that?
- Colorado, moron.

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:28.455
Okay. Well, why are we moving there?

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:29.993
Somebody told me
about it once.

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:32.723
They said it was the most
beautiful place they'd seen.

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:34.833
It's on this hill.
Or is it a mountain?

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:37.026
Maybe it's on a hill by a mountain.
Anyway...

00:05:37.204 --> 00:05:39.901
...I was thinking we should move there.
What do you say?

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:42.838
- l say that's not even a reason!
- I know. How great is that?

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.979
- We'd be moving for no reason.
- That's not great. That's crazy!

00:05:46.146 --> 00:05:48.240
That's Harrison Ford
in Mosquito Coast crazy.

00:05:48.415 --> 00:05:51.510
You say crazy. It might be
the sanest thing I've ever done.

00:05:51.685 --> 00:05:54.518
I want this to be a democratic decision,
so we're gonna vote.

00:05:54.688 --> 00:05:56.952
Everyone who wants to move...

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:59.353
...and get their own horse
raise your hand.

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:03.592
- Well, that decides it.
- Democratic? You bought her vote!

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:06.232
Yeah. That's the American version.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.297
I want you to remember this.

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:10.698
This is the moment
you conspired with a psycho...

00:06:10.871 --> 00:06:14.068
...to ruin whatever was left
of our pathetic little lives.

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:17.200
As it turns out...

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:20.677
...Andy's leaving caused quite a stir
in the medical community.

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:22.576
TIME magazine
even wrote about it...

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:25.218
...calling Andrew Brown's
departure from neurosurgery:

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:28.082
"One of the great losses
of modern medicine."

00:06:28.255 --> 00:06:31.520
Like a lot of people, you might think
they were exaggerating.

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:36.151
But then, you probably
don't know Dr. Brown.

00:07:02.289 --> 00:07:07.455
Everwood, Colorado. Population,
fust over 9000 and growing.

00:07:07.627 --> 00:07:11.291
Founded in 1853,
this jewel of the Centennial State...

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:14.866
...is home to one of the country's
first opera houses...

00:07:15.035 --> 00:07:18.471
...oldest gold mines,
third largest chili cook-off...

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:22.575
...and even the occasional
world-famous brain surgeon.

00:07:24.511 --> 00:07:25.808
Son of a--

00:07:25.979 --> 00:07:27.811
Guess.

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:29.776
- Rangers.
- Nope.

00:07:31.084 --> 00:07:33.109
Rockies. Somebody's acclimating.

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:36.220
- Getting adjusted.
- Do I have to eat these?

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:38.585
- They don't smell right.
- You're in luck, we're late.

00:07:38.758 --> 00:07:40.749
But I want you to drink that orange juice.

00:07:40.927 --> 00:07:45.728
Dad, Ephram read that high doses
of vitamin C cause blindness in lab rats.

00:07:45.899 --> 00:07:47.890
- Does Ephram have a medical degree?
- No.

00:07:48.068 --> 00:07:50.332
- Do I?
- l1 see where you're taking this.

00:07:51.771 --> 00:07:52.966
There's your bus.

00:07:54.774 --> 00:07:56.970
- Where's my lunch?
- Lunch?

00:07:57.978 --> 00:08:00.504
I forgot to make it.
Tell you what. Here.

00:08:00.914 --> 00:08:02.439
Here's some cash.

00:08:02.615 --> 00:08:06.449
- I don't think they'll change a 50.
- Okay, here's some singles.

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:12.049
I forgot. You want to do this alone.

00:08:12.459 --> 00:08:14.985
It's a big step for me.
Love you.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.298
I love you too, kiddo.

00:08:30.143 --> 00:08:32.805
Rosemary Clooney.
My, my, my.

00:08:32.979 --> 00:08:34.640
It's Delia Brown.

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:37.408
I know.
Rosemary Clooney's on the radio.

00:08:37.584 --> 00:08:41.282
I take note of what's playing when a
passenger enters my bus for the first time.

00:08:41.454 --> 00:08:42.944
It tells me something
about them.

00:08:43.123 --> 00:08:44.648
What's Maryrose Clooney tell you?

00:08:45.058 --> 00:08:48.323
She tells me that you
and I are gonna get on just fine.

00:08:49.662 --> 00:08:51.494
The kids call me Mr. Irv.

00:08:57.637 --> 00:08:59.799
- Let's get you to school.
- I'm riding my bike.

00:08:59.973 --> 00:09:02.203
- Why? I can drive you.
- l1 appreciate the offer...

00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:04.605
...but it's about 10 years too late.

00:09:20.927 --> 00:09:22.588
You're not a plant.

00:09:22.796 --> 00:09:25.322
- I'm a boy!
- Impressive.

00:09:25.498 --> 00:09:28.092
I see you've met
my resident horticulturalist.

00:09:28.635 --> 00:09:30.763
Honey, why don't you go inside.
It's cold.

00:09:32.005 --> 00:09:35.600
Nina Feeney. And that monster is Samuel.
We're your neighbors.

00:09:35.775 --> 00:09:38.107
That's a weird coincidence,
I'm your neighbor.

00:09:38.278 --> 00:09:40.713
- Dr. Brown, right?
- Please, Andy.

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:43.247
- And how did you--?
- Oh, small town, Andy.

00:09:43.716 --> 00:09:47.152
If you'll excuse me, I have to ship him
to daycare. Nice meeting you.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.515
Nice to meet you, Nina.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:58.628
Nice hair color.

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:03.301
Hey, freak.
What's with the hair, man?

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:05.598
- They run out of green at the store?
- Hey, you.

00:10:05.772 --> 00:10:08.173
My friend asked you a question.
Where's your manners?

00:10:08.341 --> 00:10:09.934
I'm sorry.
I didn't understand him.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:11.839
You see,
I don't speak dumb-ass.

00:10:12.011 --> 00:10:15.345
But since you obviously do,
maybe you could translate for me.

00:10:28.628 --> 00:10:29.925
Hey.

00:10:30.096 --> 00:10:32.292
- Hey.
- You were bold out there.

00:10:32.465 --> 00:10:35.901
- Oh, it was just strategy, really.
- Strategy?

00:10:36.069 --> 00:10:39.937
I find it best when dealing with any
unfamiliar bully to strike early with sarcasm.

00:10:40.106 --> 00:10:42.768
Makes them wonder if I have
secret butt-kicking prowess...

00:10:42.942 --> 00:10:46.276
- ...they're unable to detect.
- Wow, you really have this thought out.

00:10:46.446 --> 00:10:50.713
Spend as much time inside a gym locker as
me, you'd have a few theories of your own.

00:10:50.884 --> 00:10:54.286
- Were they that horrible in New York?
- How'd you know I was from New York?

00:10:54.454 --> 00:10:56.718
That doctor who moved here.
He's your father.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:59.188
Yeah, if you use the term "father" loosely.

00:10:59.359 --> 00:11:02.590
Ever since that article in 7/ME,
he's all anyone can talk about here.

00:11:02.762 --> 00:11:04.628
Yeah?
Well, what do they say?

00:11:05.398 --> 00:11:07.696
Mostly they just wonder
why he came.

00:11:07.867 --> 00:11:10.427
If they figure it out, let me know.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:12.597
You don't know why you came here?

00:11:12.772 --> 00:11:15.241
- Whacked, I know.
- I think it's wild.

00:11:15.408 --> 00:11:18.503
Sometimes I wonder if my dad's
the most boring man alive.

00:11:19.746 --> 00:11:20.941
There's the bell.

00:11:21.114 --> 00:11:23.242
We should eat lunch sometime.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.082
Wait.

00:11:27.053 --> 00:11:30.045
- What's your name?
- Amy.

00:11:30.223 --> 00:11:32.248
And I like your hair.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:40.957
If you like the house, you are sure
to absolutely adore these offices.

00:11:41.134 --> 00:11:43.159
Mrs. Baxworth, why is everyone
staring at us?

00:11:43.336 --> 00:11:46.636
Not us. You.
You're quite the celebrity in town.

00:11:46.806 --> 00:11:49.036
- Celebrity?
- There's been all sorts of chatter...

00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:51.701
...about what brings you
to our corner of the world.

00:11:51.878 --> 00:11:55.872
- Saw it on a map.
- "Saw it on a map." Such a kidder.

00:11:56.049 --> 00:11:58.780
Seriously, I don't want to pry,
but everyone's wondering...

00:11:58.952 --> 00:12:01.387
...what kind of practice
you're gonna set up here.

00:12:01.554 --> 00:12:05.115
There's been some talk that you're here
to do some top-secret brain research.

00:12:05.291 --> 00:12:07.919
I'm just opening up
a general practice.

00:12:08.962 --> 00:12:11.021
Why? Is there a problem with that?

00:12:12.932 --> 00:12:16.664
You are aware that we already
have a family doctor in town?

00:12:16.836 --> 00:12:18.634
Oh, sure. I assume there must be.

00:12:18.805 --> 00:12:21.467
But surely a town
can use two doctors.

00:12:21.841 --> 00:12:24.367
Of course we can!

00:12:24.544 --> 00:12:26.512
Hey, doc! Doc!

00:12:26.679 --> 00:12:29.307
I've been waiting for you.
Right on time.

00:12:30.083 --> 00:12:31.482
How are you today, Dr. Abbott?

00:12:31.651 --> 00:12:33.847
- Just fine, Mr. Greeley.
- That makes one of us.

00:12:34.988 --> 00:12:37.753
- And how are you today, Mr. Greeley?
- I'm so glad you asked.

00:12:37.924 --> 00:12:40.552
There's a pain in my left leg,
just above the knee.

00:12:40.727 --> 00:12:42.889
- A throbbing pain or a sharp pain?
- Throbbing.

00:12:43.062 --> 00:12:45.224
No, no. Sharp.
No. Throbbing.

00:12:45.398 --> 00:12:48.732
- How long have you had it?
- About three years.

00:12:48.901 --> 00:12:51.302
I have an opening this Friday,
around 2:15.

00:12:51.471 --> 00:12:53.166
Couldn't you just
check me out here?

00:12:53.339 --> 00:12:57.936
As I've explained to you before, there are
insurance regulations that prohibit me...

00:12:58.111 --> 00:13:00.671
...from diagnosing you
without a proper checkup.

00:13:00.847 --> 00:13:04.215
- But it's just a little pain.
- A little pain can become a big lawsuit.

00:13:04.384 --> 00:13:07.217
Let's say, hypothetically,
I were to misdiagnose you now...

00:13:07.387 --> 00:13:10.789
...with an osteoarthritic condition
and advise you to purchase aspirin.

00:13:10.957 --> 00:13:13.790
You adhere to my suggestion,
and this evening, you drop dead--

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:19.694
Again, hypothetically, of a brain disorder
expressing itself unilaterally in your left leg.

00:13:19.866 --> 00:13:23.962
Can you imagine the malpractice case
that your family would have against me?

00:13:24.137 --> 00:13:26.936
Sorry, I don't make the rules.
I just live by them.

00:13:27.106 --> 00:13:28.596
Friday, 2:15, then.

00:13:32.478 --> 00:13:34.947
Three examining rooms
back here.

00:13:35.114 --> 00:13:37.276
Spacious reception area.

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:40.112
- Just like in the big city, huh?
- That's just the problem.

00:13:40.286 --> 00:13:44.450
I spent my life in this office. This is exactly
the office I'm trying to get away from.

00:13:44.624 --> 00:13:46.991
Did I mention this has DSL capability?

00:13:47.527 --> 00:13:49.325
Do you smell that?

00:13:49.495 --> 00:13:50.860
Smell what?

00:13:51.197 --> 00:13:54.792
- Perfume.
- Oh, Estée Lauder, White Linen.

00:13:54.967 --> 00:13:57.561
No, no.
This is coming from the street.

00:14:00.673 --> 00:14:02.334
It's called Jeanette.

00:14:02.508 --> 00:14:05.500
It was popular in Europe
in the early '80s.

00:14:05.745 --> 00:14:08.771
A wealthy Frenchman had the
fragrance named for his fiancée.

00:14:08.948 --> 00:14:11.076
Only after she died,
he had it discontinued...

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:15.949
...which made it increasingly difficult
to surprise my wife with every Christmas.

00:14:16.222 --> 00:14:17.451
It was her favorite.

00:14:18.224 --> 00:14:21.751
You mean you smell
your deceased wife?

00:14:21.928 --> 00:14:23.623
Look at this.

00:14:24.931 --> 00:14:26.160
What is this place?

00:14:26.332 --> 00:14:28.391
This offensive monstrosity?

00:14:28.568 --> 00:14:31.003
It was the train depot
till the city shut it down.

00:14:31.237 --> 00:14:32.898
- Shut it down?
- About 10 years ago...

00:14:33.072 --> 00:14:36.007
...the railroad decided to re-route the train
through Central City.

00:14:36.175 --> 00:14:39.304
They said it was a safer approach
through the mountains.

00:14:39.479 --> 00:14:41.743
Everwood doesn't have
a train running through?

00:14:41.914 --> 00:14:45.748
I'm afraid we've ceased
being a destination.

00:14:46.652 --> 00:14:48.484
Not to everybody.

00:15:03.302 --> 00:15:07.330
I'd be careful. You never know what
animal might have taken refuge in here.

00:15:07.507 --> 00:15:09.498
Or God forbid, a hobo.

00:15:11.944 --> 00:15:13.241
You see what I see?

00:15:13.413 --> 00:15:16.576
Multiple opportunities
for staph infection?

00:15:16.749 --> 00:15:18.649
No, Mrs. Baxworth.

00:15:19.585 --> 00:15:21.553
My new office.

00:15:41.574 --> 00:15:45.442
The most important thing about manga
is it's different than American comics...

00:15:45.611 --> 00:15:47.807
...in every way, shape, form.

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:50.608
I mean, forget style.
It's more than aesthetics.

00:15:50.783 --> 00:15:52.376
The manga-ka.
The writers of manga.

00:15:52.552 --> 00:15:55.647
They write heroes who are
someone's kid or someone's boss.

00:15:55.822 --> 00:16:00.282
The hero's civilian life is as important
to the story as their secret identity.

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:04.897
It's not just Clark Kent
waiting to turn into Superman.

00:16:05.398 --> 00:16:08.163
It's Superman...

00:16:08.334 --> 00:16:10.496
...waiting to turn into Clark Kent.

00:16:12.271 --> 00:16:15.297
I never knew comics
could be so hot.

00:16:15.475 --> 00:16:17.170
Hot?

00:16:18.845 --> 00:16:21.371
Have you ever had
a perfect make out song?

00:16:22.548 --> 00:16:23.811
Several, really.

00:16:36.062 --> 00:16:38.656
Mine's Al Green's
"Let's Stay Together."

00:16:38.831 --> 00:16:41.664
I think it speaks
to a girl's dual desires...

00:16:41.834 --> 00:16:45.702
...to be held and ravaged
simultaneously.

00:16:46.405 --> 00:16:49.466
Not in a literal sense.
It's more primal.

00:16:49.642 --> 00:16:54.136
Just listening to the song right now
makes me want to take off my clothes....

00:16:56.782 --> 00:16:59.752
Right here?
I mean, in front of everybody?

00:16:59.919 --> 00:17:01.512
Why not?

00:17:19.906 --> 00:17:21.431
Damn it.

00:17:23.042 --> 00:17:24.567
What are you doing in here?

00:17:24.744 --> 00:17:27.111
What does one normally do
in the laundry room?

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:30.011
- Since when do you do your own laundry?
- I spilt something on my sheets.

00:17:30.182 --> 00:17:33.083
- What did you spill?
- Chocolate milk.

00:17:33.252 --> 00:17:38.452
- When did we get chocolate milk?
- I don't know. Stop asking me questions.

00:17:40.826 --> 00:17:44.126
- I'm making pancakes. You want some?
- Go to hell!

00:17:44.297 --> 00:17:46.197
That's my boy.

00:18:03.816 --> 00:18:05.250
Excuse me.

00:18:06.252 --> 00:18:07.651
Excuse me!

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:09.083
Excuse me!

00:18:10.289 --> 00:18:11.848
Excuse me.

00:18:12.024 --> 00:18:13.321
Yeah, can I help you?

00:18:13.492 --> 00:18:16.518
- Yeah, you're parked in my spot.
- Your spot?

00:18:16.696 --> 00:18:19.427
That's your black,
foreign-made sports utility vehicle...

00:18:19.599 --> 00:18:21.533
...with the New York plates, is it not?

00:18:21.701 --> 00:18:23.567
- Yes, itis.
- It's in my spot.

00:18:23.736 --> 00:18:25.534
Park there again, I'll have it towed.

00:18:25.705 --> 00:18:28.333
I'm sorry.
I didn't see a name on the curb.

00:18:28.507 --> 00:18:31.340
It's implied.
It's in front of my office.

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:34.104
You're the other doctor.
How do you do? I'm Andy Brown.

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:36.112
I know who you are.

00:18:36.282 --> 00:18:39.684
And if by "other doctor," you meant
Everwood's primary care physician...

00:18:39.852 --> 00:18:41.616
...yes, that's me.

00:18:42.321 --> 00:18:46.019
- Some golfing weather, huh?
- I happen to belong to an indoor range.

00:18:46.192 --> 00:18:48.456
- Is that driver Titleist?
- It is.

00:18:48.628 --> 00:18:50.995
Expensive. Can I see it?

00:18:51.163 --> 00:18:54.656
Be careful. That club was used
by none other than Tiger Woods himself...

00:18:54.834 --> 00:18:57.030
...in the '99 British Open.

00:18:57.203 --> 00:19:00.901
- Purchased it on eBay.
- No kidding? I'll have to tell him.

00:19:02.341 --> 00:19:06.300
- You know Tiger Woods?
- I1 operated on his uncle. Sweet kid.

00:19:06.479 --> 00:19:09.972
About this whole office thing,
I'm not here to step on your turf.

00:19:10.149 --> 00:19:13.312
My turf? That's rich.
Nobody told you, did they?

00:19:13.486 --> 00:19:15.215
- What?
- l wouldn't waste your time...

00:19:15.388 --> 00:19:18.358
...turning this place into a doctor's office.
No one will use it.

00:19:18.524 --> 00:19:19.514
Why is that?

00:19:19.692 --> 00:19:22.286
That building over there
will continue to receive...

00:19:22.461 --> 00:19:24.555
...all of the patients in this community.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:26.255
The flower mart?

00:19:26.432 --> 00:19:29.527
- The other one. My doctor's office.
- How do you figure?

00:19:29.702 --> 00:19:31.636
Because while you have been operating...

00:19:31.804 --> 00:19:34.535
...on Tiger's uncle
and getting you picture in 7/ME...

00:19:34.707 --> 00:19:38.007
...I have been the doctor
in this community for over 15 years.

00:19:38.177 --> 00:19:40.009
Before me, it was my father.

00:19:40.246 --> 00:19:43.876
Was it your father's father before him?
Because that would be really cool.

00:19:44.050 --> 00:19:46.018
Do what you want, sir.

00:19:46.185 --> 00:19:48.677
I'm just advising you
not to waste your time.

00:19:48.854 --> 00:19:52.051
I appreciate your concern, but I came
a long way to open this office.

00:19:52.224 --> 00:19:54.693
- Nothing's gonna stop me.
- In that case...

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:56.726
...happy painting.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:58.961
Nice meeting you.

00:19:59.131 --> 00:20:00.530
Nut bag.

00:20:06.505 --> 00:20:08.234
We're almost there.

00:20:08.407 --> 00:20:11.240
- I told you you're gonna love this place.
- Yeah.

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:13.708
I'd love it even more
if it were indoors.

00:20:13.879 --> 00:20:15.608
Okay, you ready?

00:20:16.248 --> 00:20:17.875
Look.

00:20:18.517 --> 00:20:20.383
You can see the whole town from here.

00:20:20.553 --> 00:20:23.215
There's Main Street
and the grade school.

00:20:23.389 --> 00:20:26.256
The factories are all that way.
And that's the church row.

00:20:26.425 --> 00:20:29.258
Episcopalian, Presbyterian,
Catholic, Lutheran and Baptist.

00:20:29.428 --> 00:20:31.556
- Where's the synagogue?
- Are you Jewish?

00:20:32.264 --> 00:20:33.959
Half. My mom is--

00:20:36.402 --> 00:20:37.665
Was.

00:20:38.003 --> 00:20:40.438
- Sorry.
- About what?

00:20:40.873 --> 00:20:43.638
- I didn't mean for the topic to come up.
- No biggie.

00:20:43.809 --> 00:20:45.800
Talking about her
is pretty unavoidable.

00:20:45.978 --> 00:20:48.675
What with her
giving birth to me and all.

00:20:55.921 --> 00:20:58.856
So did your dad really work on a king?

00:21:00.359 --> 00:21:05.092
He was just a prince at the time,
but sure.

00:21:06.165 --> 00:21:07.530
What's it like?

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.465
Having a dad who's famous?

00:21:12.271 --> 00:21:14.638
It's like this.
You're 8 years old.

00:21:14.807 --> 00:21:17.401
He misses your birthday party.
You want to cry about it.

00:21:17.576 --> 00:21:20.705
But he's on TV that night for separating
the heads of Siamese twins.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:23.440
You're 10. He's not there
to see you in the school play.

00:21:23.616 --> 00:21:27.382
He is in The New York Times
for restoring the vision of a 5-year-old kid.

00:21:27.553 --> 00:21:29.453
You know that prince
that you mentioned?

00:21:29.622 --> 00:21:31.317
I think of him as my dad's excuse...

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:33.686
...for missing my elementary-school
graduation.

00:21:33.859 --> 00:21:38.126
You want to be mad at him,
you want to hate him, but you can't.

00:21:38.497 --> 00:21:40.761
He's saving lives.

00:21:46.438 --> 00:21:47.963
Amy, why are you talking to me?

00:21:49.375 --> 00:21:51.070
- What?
- Where I come from...

00:21:51.243 --> 00:21:53.541
...girls like you don't breathe
around guys like me...

00:21:53.712 --> 00:21:55.373
...without having some secret agenda.

00:21:55.548 --> 00:22:00.418
- Mine's world domination.
- Seriously. I mean...

00:22:00.586 --> 00:22:03.055
...you seem like
you have enough friends.

00:22:03.422 --> 00:22:05.550
Why go out of your way
to make me feel welcome?

00:22:05.724 --> 00:22:09.820
You've got kind of a tragic,
lonely thing going on.

00:22:10.229 --> 00:22:11.560
1 dig it.

00:22:12.565 --> 00:22:14.761
You don't happen to listen
to Al Green, do you?

00:22:14.934 --> 00:22:16.333
Who's Al Green?

00:22:26.812 --> 00:22:28.837
Oh, I should get to class.

00:22:29.014 --> 00:22:32.609
- Okay. All right, see you later.
- Bye.

00:22:37.056 --> 00:22:40.617
Dad's gonna skin your ass when he finds
out you're hanging out with that kid.

00:22:40.793 --> 00:22:43.353
Dad's not finding out,
because you're not telling him.

00:22:43.529 --> 00:22:44.587
- Aren't I?
- No.

00:22:44.763 --> 00:22:47.733
Not if you value that collection
of porn stashed on our computer.

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:49.334
What was the file name again?

00:22:49.501 --> 00:22:52.163
Oh, yeah.
"Favorite biblical passages."

00:22:54.373 --> 00:22:56.967
Dude, she is smooth.

00:23:02.615 --> 00:23:04.174
It's crooked.

00:23:04.350 --> 00:23:08.878
Sure, if you look at it straight on.
But if you lean a little bit, it's perfect. See?

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:17.927
- You Doc Brown?
- Yes, I am.

00:23:18.097 --> 00:23:20.191
You're scrawnier
than your picture.

00:23:20.733 --> 00:23:23.634
Nice to meet you, Sparky.
Name's Edna Harper.

00:23:23.802 --> 00:23:26.737
- Hello, Edna.
- Who's the private first class?

00:23:26.906 --> 00:23:28.203
I'm Delia.

00:23:28.374 --> 00:23:31.435
Word on the front is, you're turning this
into a doctor's office.

00:23:31.610 --> 00:23:33.669
If so, I've come
to inquire about employ.

00:23:33.846 --> 00:23:36.372
- What do you do?
- Forty years' nursing experience.

00:23:36.548 --> 00:23:38.448
That includes
two tours of Nam.

00:23:38.617 --> 00:23:41.086
Army nurse corps.
Thrice decorated.

00:23:41.253 --> 00:23:44.655
Here's a résumé. I'm sure
you'll find it to your satisfaction.

00:23:44.823 --> 00:23:47.315
- You worked for Dr. Abbott?
- Senior and junior.

00:23:47.493 --> 00:23:48.858
Why'd you leave?

00:23:49.028 --> 00:23:52.157
An unfortunate incident,
the details I'd rather not divulge...

00:23:52.331 --> 00:23:54.493
...on account of they're
of a personal nature.

00:23:54.667 --> 00:23:57.034
I can assure you, however,
the parting was mutual.

00:23:57.202 --> 00:24:00.103
Well, why don't I look at this
and call you later in the week.

00:24:00.272 --> 00:24:02.240
Will do.
See you around, doc.

00:24:02.408 --> 00:24:04.570
Adiés, private.

00:24:22.962 --> 00:24:24.726
- Stop it!
- It just sits here.

00:24:24.897 --> 00:24:26.865
- No one touches it.
- I said, stop it.

00:24:27.032 --> 00:24:29.763
- Dad!
- That's enough, both of you.

00:24:29.935 --> 00:24:33.394
Go upstairs, get ready for bed.
I'll be up in a few minutes to read to you.

00:24:33.572 --> 00:24:35.199
- But I want to--
- Go on.

00:24:36.642 --> 00:24:39.134
She does have a point, you know.

00:24:39.311 --> 00:24:41.245
You gotta start playing again sometime.

00:24:41.413 --> 00:24:42.710
You're right.

00:24:42.881 --> 00:24:44.906
- l am?
- Yes, Father.

00:24:45.851 --> 00:24:48.980
For it is only through the gift of music
that I can heal the pain...

00:24:49.154 --> 00:24:51.145
...that grows deep within me.

00:24:51.757 --> 00:24:53.782
Like you ever cared
if I played or not.

00:25:19.918 --> 00:25:21.784
What did you say to him?

00:25:22.488 --> 00:25:25.617
- Who?
- Mr. Warren. About his wife.

00:25:27.059 --> 00:25:28.891
What could I say?

00:25:29.061 --> 00:25:31.291
She died on my watch.

00:25:32.331 --> 00:25:35.426
On top of that, the poor guy
was left with a family to raise.

00:25:35.601 --> 00:25:36.966
Guess how many kids.

00:25:37.970 --> 00:25:40.064
- Three.
- Six.

00:25:40.239 --> 00:25:43.038
And for a single dad,
that's six kids too many.

00:25:44.610 --> 00:25:47.079
- You should grow a beard.
- You've said that for years.

00:25:47.246 --> 00:25:49.943
- You'd look distinguished.
- I'd look like my uncle Norman.

00:25:50.115 --> 00:25:53.551
- Your uncle Norman looks distinguished.
- You've got a thing for my uncle?

00:25:53.719 --> 00:25:55.414
Do you ever think about it?
You must.

00:25:55.587 --> 00:25:57.385
You and my uncle Norman?
I try not to.

00:25:57.556 --> 00:26:00.025
- What you'd do if you were left alone.
- That's morbid.

00:26:00.192 --> 00:26:01.887
It's important we talk about it.

00:26:02.061 --> 00:26:05.929
No, you're not gonna exercise the spousal
"it's important we talk about it" clause.

00:26:06.098 --> 00:26:09.500
- Why not?
- Because I'm tired, I've had a 16-hour day.

00:26:09.668 --> 00:26:12.262
These conversations
always end up getting me in trouble.

00:26:12.438 --> 00:26:16.341
And as far as hypothetical tragedies go,
can't we start with a lesser one?

00:26:16.508 --> 00:26:20.741
Ask me what I'd do If I lost my sight
or my hearing or I could never walk again.

00:26:20.913 --> 00:26:25.680
Ask me what I'd do if I could never see
another Yankees game or eat another pizza.

00:26:27.319 --> 00:26:29.583
But don't ask me
what I'd do without you.

00:26:30.989 --> 00:26:32.684
I hate when you do that.

00:26:32.858 --> 00:26:35.520
- Say the right thing?
- Attempt to say the right thing.

00:26:35.694 --> 00:26:38.720
The actual right thing
would have been far less cheesy.

00:26:45.838 --> 00:26:47.772
What are you doing?

00:26:49.441 --> 00:26:53.275
Certain cultures refer to this motion
as dancing.

00:26:54.279 --> 00:26:56.509
But there's no music.

00:26:58.317 --> 00:27:00.217
Yes, there is.

00:27:01.386 --> 00:27:03.377
There's Gershwin.

00:27:05.124 --> 00:27:07.218
And there's Sinatra.

00:27:08.193 --> 00:27:12.926
And I think there's even a little Dionne
Warwick thrown in, but I can't be sure.

00:27:16.235 --> 00:27:17.600
I know...

00:27:19.104 --> 00:27:20.629
...me too.

00:27:46.632 --> 00:27:49.067
- Good morning, doctor.
- It was.

00:27:50.636 --> 00:27:52.229
You know,
your office is back there.

00:27:52.404 --> 00:27:54.566
I know where it is.
I'm getting a cup of coffee.

00:27:54.740 --> 00:27:57.869
I was thinking last night.
You look vaguely familiar to me.

00:27:58.043 --> 00:28:00.512
Perhaps I remind you of one
of the inmates you knew...

00:28:00.679 --> 00:28:04.206
- ...at whatever asylum you escaped from.
- It's my first day. Wish me luck?

00:28:04.383 --> 00:28:07.148
Oh, it'll take more than luck
to launch the U.S.S. Wacko.

00:28:07.319 --> 00:28:09.651
But what the hey.
Good luck.

00:28:09.821 --> 00:28:13.451
Now, if you're done blathering,
one of us has patients to attend to.

00:28:13.625 --> 00:28:16.117
- Have a nice day.
- Whatever.

00:28:29.508 --> 00:28:31.203
Yes.

00:28:37.449 --> 00:28:40.111
Edna Harper,
what are you doing here?

00:28:40.285 --> 00:28:41.946
Let's see. I'm in a doctor's office.

00:28:42.120 --> 00:28:44.111
I'm wearing my nurse whites.
My taxes?

00:28:44.289 --> 00:28:46.155
Does Doc Abbott know
you're working here?

00:28:46.325 --> 00:28:47.986
- Nope.
- He will now.

00:28:48.160 --> 00:28:50.595
Mrs. Baxworth,
how are you this fine day?

00:28:50.762 --> 00:28:53.561
Just fine. I came to wish
you well on your new venture.

00:28:53.732 --> 00:28:56.997
- I brought you a plant.
- Well, thank you. That's very kind of you.

00:28:57.169 --> 00:29:00.332
My. my. Just look what you
have done with this place.

00:29:00.505 --> 00:29:02.030
Something wrong
with your neck?

00:29:02.207 --> 00:29:03.868
It's just been
a little stiff lately.

00:29:04.042 --> 00:29:06.067
Want me to take a look at it?

00:29:06.845 --> 00:29:10.406
Oh, I would. I've already made an
appointment tomorrow with Doc Abbott.

00:29:10.582 --> 00:29:13.244
Why put off till tomorrow
what you can diagnose today?

00:29:13.418 --> 00:29:15.386
- It's not that I don't trust you.
- My loss.

00:29:15.554 --> 00:29:18.251
It'd be like examining
Ms. Taylor all over again.

00:29:18.890 --> 00:29:22.224
- Excuse me?
- You see how your clavicle rises up here?

00:29:22.394 --> 00:29:25.796
Typically, the lateral end is flat,
but yours has a perfect S shape.

00:29:25.964 --> 00:29:28.899
The only other time I've seen that
was on Elizabeth Taylor.

00:29:29.568 --> 00:29:31.297
You operated on Liz Taylor?

00:29:31.470 --> 00:29:33.768
I confess.

00:29:33.939 --> 00:29:35.771
Maybe you should
take a look at my neck.

00:29:35.941 --> 00:29:38.967
I mean, I'm sure
Doc Abbott wouldn't mind.

00:29:39.144 --> 00:29:40.942
Oh, my goodness gracious.

00:29:52.858 --> 00:29:57.091
It's not often I find a third-grader lost
in profound thought on their lunch hour.

00:29:57.262 --> 00:29:59.356
Hey, Mr. Irv. I don't feel good.

00:29:59.531 --> 00:30:00.862
Yeah?

00:30:01.033 --> 00:30:02.762
Why is that?

00:30:02.934 --> 00:30:04.163
Can you keep a secret?

00:30:04.336 --> 00:30:05.861
I can.

00:30:06.038 --> 00:30:07.369
I think my dad's sick.

00:30:07.539 --> 00:30:11.169
He talks to himself,
to my mom like she's still here.

00:30:11.343 --> 00:30:15.211
Only that's a problem
because she died eight months ago.

00:30:16.915 --> 00:30:19.543
I'm not gonna lie to you, Delia.

00:30:19.718 --> 00:30:22.312
Sounds like your dad's
got a case of something.

00:30:22.487 --> 00:30:25.047
- I knew it.
- But what he has...

00:30:25.223 --> 00:30:29.182
...it's the one sickness most people
spend their whole life trying to catch.

00:30:29.361 --> 00:30:31.125
What does he have?

00:30:31.296 --> 00:30:33.390
A distraught heart.

00:30:33.565 --> 00:30:36.159
It's not like other diseases.
It can't kill you.

00:30:36.335 --> 00:30:38.394
Just the opposite, in fact.

00:30:38.570 --> 00:30:43.633
In most cases, it makes a person
feel alive for the first time.

00:30:43.809 --> 00:30:46.005
Only problem is...

00:30:46.178 --> 00:30:49.671
...there's no remedy for it
anywhere in the world.

00:30:53.085 --> 00:30:55.247
As I suspected,
a mild case of torticollis...

00:30:55.420 --> 00:30:57.548
...brought on, my guess
would be, by a new bed.

00:30:57.723 --> 00:30:59.782
I just bought a new California king.

00:30:59.958 --> 00:31:01.653
It might take some getting used to.

00:31:01.827 --> 00:31:04.319
Until then, I'm gonna prescribe
you a muscle relaxant.

00:31:04.496 --> 00:31:07.295
Edna will get you a neck brace.
Wear it if the pain gets worse.

00:31:07.466 --> 00:31:10.492
I didn't bring my purse.
How about I run you by a check later?

00:31:10.669 --> 00:31:11.966
I'm not charging you.

00:31:12.137 --> 00:31:15.038
For the neck brace, fine.
But for the visit, I have my--

00:31:15.207 --> 00:31:16.971
I'm not charging
anyone for anything.

00:31:17.142 --> 00:31:18.974
My services are free.

00:31:19.611 --> 00:31:21.238
Free?

00:31:23.014 --> 00:31:25.608
- As in--
- No cash, no checks, no credit cards.

00:31:25.784 --> 00:31:27.912
Not even Discover.

00:31:28.086 --> 00:31:29.747
Well, what will you do for income?

00:31:29.921 --> 00:31:31.719
I was a brain surgeon
for 15 years.

00:31:31.890 --> 00:31:33.688
I have a few pennies tucked away.

00:31:33.859 --> 00:31:36.055
Here's that prescription.

00:31:36.228 --> 00:31:37.855
Okay. Well...

00:31:39.164 --> 00:31:41.428
...I'm off to the pharmacy.

00:31:41.600 --> 00:31:42.897
Toodles.

00:31:43.468 --> 00:31:45.596
You realize by telling her
what you told her...

00:31:45.771 --> 00:31:48.001
...you told the whole town.

00:31:48.173 --> 00:31:49.902
You don't say?

00:31:57.616 --> 00:31:59.311
Looking for Amy?

00:31:59.551 --> 00:32:00.916
She's not coming.

00:32:01.086 --> 00:32:04.283
- And you are?
- Her brother. I left you that note.

00:32:04.456 --> 00:32:07.016
- l wanted to talk to you.
- You could have talked to me.

00:32:07.192 --> 00:32:09.991
You didn't have to go to the trouble
of imitating feminine cursive.

00:32:10.162 --> 00:32:12.324
- That's my real handwriting.
- Whoops.

00:32:12.531 --> 00:32:15.831
Stay away from Amy.
She's got a boyfriend. She tell you that?

00:32:16.001 --> 00:32:20.336
No, but she didn't talk about you either,
so we only covered the important stuff.

00:32:21.072 --> 00:32:22.506
Hey, nice bag.

00:32:22.674 --> 00:32:24.335
- Wonder what's in it.
- Give me that.

00:32:27.245 --> 00:32:28.906
Ita?

00:32:29.080 --> 00:32:30.809
This stuff's way expensive, man.

00:32:32.517 --> 00:32:34.315
What do you say
we double its value?

00:32:34.486 --> 00:32:36.113
Bright, stop it.

00:32:37.489 --> 00:32:39.048
Bright?

00:32:39.224 --> 00:32:41.318
That's his name?
Ironic.

00:32:41.493 --> 00:32:43.894
Go ahead.
Tell him why you're hanging out with him.

00:32:45.096 --> 00:32:47.394
- Ephram, I can explain.
- Forget it.

00:32:47.566 --> 00:32:49.591
There's nothing to say.
Don't worry, Bright.

00:32:49.768 --> 00:32:52.203
I'll be staying away
from your sister...

00:32:52.370 --> 00:32:54.031
...for good.

00:32:54.206 --> 00:32:55.833
By the way, dude, nice dad.

00:32:56.007 --> 00:32:59.568
Has he always been such a headcase
or just since your mom bought it?

00:33:03.615 --> 00:33:07.051
Bright.
Bright, get off him!

00:33:16.728 --> 00:33:18.162
Ephram.

00:33:18.330 --> 00:33:19.820
You okay?

00:33:21.199 --> 00:33:24.396
- What's going on?
- I don't want to talk about it.

00:33:28.840 --> 00:33:30.535
You.

00:33:31.142 --> 00:33:35.079
Well, I should have known it was one
of your offspring that did this to my son.

00:33:35.247 --> 00:33:36.942
Wait. You guys know each other?

00:33:39.150 --> 00:33:40.515
My sister forgot to tell you?

00:33:40.685 --> 00:33:44.246
- My dad's the real doctor in this town.
- Come on. Let's go, kids.

00:33:44.856 --> 00:33:46.415
Before I set a bad example.

00:33:51.196 --> 00:33:52.664
Come on.

00:34:00.505 --> 00:34:02.098
So...

00:34:02.707 --> 00:34:04.471
...what do you got to say
for yourself?

00:34:04.643 --> 00:34:06.133
Give it up.

00:34:06.311 --> 00:34:09.144
Ephram, I thought you'd change.
I thought if we moved here...

00:34:09.314 --> 00:34:13.342
- ...you'd stop the fighting, the acting out.
- I got this black eye because of you...

00:34:13.518 --> 00:34:14.883
...dick.

00:34:15.053 --> 00:34:17.454
Keep talking like that,
you're gonna get another one.

00:34:17.622 --> 00:34:20.648
He said you were crazy.
And you know what? News flash. You are.

00:34:20.825 --> 00:34:23.192
You quit your job,
You grow this ugly-ass beard.

00:34:23.361 --> 00:34:26.888
You look like you wear your clothes to bed
and move us to Nowheres-ville, U.S.A.

00:34:27.065 --> 00:34:30.035
And why? Because somebody
told you it was pretty once?

00:34:30.201 --> 00:34:32.966
If that's not enough,
you talk to Mom like she's still here!

00:34:33.138 --> 00:34:35.835
I've seen you. Delia too.
What do I have to say for myself?

00:34:36.007 --> 00:34:37.805
What do you have to say for yourself?

00:34:37.976 --> 00:34:41.537
- l can't believe you think my beard is ugly.
- Mom would never have done this!

00:34:41.713 --> 00:34:43.340
She never would
have moved us here!

00:34:43.515 --> 00:34:46.007
- Don't be so sure of that!
- I am sure!

00:34:46.184 --> 00:34:47.948
I knew her.
You didn't know her.

00:34:48.119 --> 00:34:50.178
You were never around.
We just tolerated you.

00:34:50.355 --> 00:34:53.347
- That's good. What else you got?
- I wish you died instead of her!

00:34:53.525 --> 00:34:56.654
- I wish I did too, you little bastard!
- l1 hate you!

00:34:56.828 --> 00:34:59.923
- I hate you back! Now get in that house!
- I'm going for a ride!

00:35:00.098 --> 00:35:01.759
- Oh, yeah?
- Yeah!

00:35:03.234 --> 00:35:06.295
At some point,
you're getting in that house!

00:35:13.979 --> 00:35:16.175
- I run a tight ship.
- So I noticed.

00:35:17.582 --> 00:35:18.811
Want a cup of coffee?

00:35:19.451 --> 00:35:21.579
Only if it's spiked.

00:35:26.958 --> 00:35:28.653
I want to apologize...

00:35:28.827 --> 00:35:31.694
...for that awful display
of parenting techniques.

00:35:32.530 --> 00:35:34.965
I'm just recently becoming
familiar with them.

00:35:35.300 --> 00:35:38.292
The only thing harder than being
a parent is being a single one.

00:35:38.470 --> 00:35:40.461
- Are you...?
- Single? No.

00:35:40.939 --> 00:35:42.202
I have a husband.

00:35:42.374 --> 00:35:44.138
A wonderful, funny and caring man...

00:35:44.309 --> 00:35:49.145
...whose flaw is he travels eight months
of the year, selling computer software.

00:35:49.314 --> 00:35:51.476
Where do you think you're going?

00:35:54.219 --> 00:35:57.154
- That's a pretty nasty cough.
- Yeah. He's had it for a month.

00:35:57.322 --> 00:36:00.519
Dr. Abbott thought it was a chest cold,
but the medicine isn't taking.

00:36:00.692 --> 00:36:03.889
- It's not getting better?
- No. But he's not getting any worse, either.

00:36:04.996 --> 00:36:06.987
What you got in the bag?

00:36:07.432 --> 00:36:10.060
- Shavel.
- It's a shovel? You know a lot.

00:36:10.935 --> 00:36:13.802
- Yeah? What's this here?
- All right...

00:36:14.639 --> 00:36:16.334
...down the hatch, tough guy.

00:36:19.144 --> 00:36:21.704
Great. Go visit your plants.

00:36:25.316 --> 00:36:28.581
You know, my wife
was the perfect parent.

00:36:28.753 --> 00:36:31.723
And that's not just revisionist
history either. She really was.

00:36:32.023 --> 00:36:33.787
Julia knew what to say.
What to do.

00:36:33.958 --> 00:36:37.087
When to talk to them.
When to ignore them.

00:36:38.663 --> 00:36:40.688
Do you know what
the foramen magnum is?

00:36:40.865 --> 00:36:42.355
Should I?

00:36:42.534 --> 00:36:45.162
It's the hole
at the base of the skull.

00:36:45.336 --> 00:36:47.361
Most doctors need
a device to find it.

00:36:47.539 --> 00:36:49.064
I never did.

00:36:49.240 --> 00:36:51.937
I could always locate it
with my hands.

00:36:53.578 --> 00:36:56.104
Surgery just came
instinctively to me.

00:36:56.948 --> 00:36:59.076
Julia was the same way
with parenting.

00:37:00.151 --> 00:37:01.915
It has to do with her, doesn't it?

00:37:02.087 --> 00:37:04.055
Why you came to Everwood?

00:37:06.124 --> 00:37:09.526
Do you believe that people
live on after they die? That...?

00:37:10.562 --> 00:37:12.052
That their souls are with us?

00:37:13.198 --> 00:37:14.927
Yeah, I do.

00:37:17.535 --> 00:37:20.470
I need to prove to my wife
that I can do this.

00:37:22.140 --> 00:37:25.872
That I can be the kind of doctor...

00:37:26.044 --> 00:37:30.174
...the kind of father that she wanted
me to be when she was alive.

00:37:31.750 --> 00:37:33.980
I know that makes me seem nuts.

00:37:34.919 --> 00:37:36.444
Maybe I am.

00:37:37.822 --> 00:37:41.156
To love someone so much you're
still proving it to them after they die?

00:37:43.795 --> 00:37:48.357
Well, if that's crazy, Andy,
I hope my own insanity isn't far away.

00:38:07.352 --> 00:38:09.218
- Good morning.
- Buzz off.

00:38:09.387 --> 00:38:12.049
And do me a favor.
Keep your son away from my daughter.

00:38:12.223 --> 00:38:15.955
- I don't think that's how it went.
- Why would Amy associate with your misfit?

00:38:16.127 --> 00:38:18.289
Well, he said something
about a crack deal.

00:38:18.997 --> 00:38:20.362
You think you're so funny.

00:38:20.532 --> 00:38:22.762
If you could get over whatever
your problem is...

00:38:22.934 --> 00:38:26.802
- ...we might teach each other a thing or two.
- What might you be able to teach me?

00:38:27.005 --> 00:38:29.474
For starters, when a 4-year-old
like Samuel Feeney...

00:38:29.641 --> 00:38:31.769
...has a chronic cough
you can't diagnose...

00:38:31.943 --> 00:38:35.277
...you might look at contributing factors
outside of the pulmonary region...

00:38:35.446 --> 00:38:37.744
...i.e., the slight cutaneous rash
on his fingertips...

00:38:37.916 --> 00:38:42.649
...an obvious sign of the fungus spore
trichosis, a.k.a., the gardener's disease.

00:38:42.821 --> 00:38:45.290
I suggest you get him off
of the cough medicine...

00:38:45.456 --> 00:38:50.860
...and on to a saturated solution of potassium
iodide before his situation worsens.

00:38:51.029 --> 00:38:52.360
Not bad for a nut bag, huh?

00:38:52.530 --> 00:38:55.795
Think that's impressive? Wait till you see
what I can do with my hands.

00:38:55.967 --> 00:38:57.833
You're so smart,
where are your patients?

00:38:58.002 --> 00:39:01.131
Actually, they're just gathering
outside my office now.

00:39:03.441 --> 00:39:06.240
Is it true?
Are your services really free of charge?

00:39:06.711 --> 00:39:08.110
Only my medical ones.

00:39:09.214 --> 00:39:10.841
You're not charging anything?

00:39:11.015 --> 00:39:12.449
- For real?
- For real.

00:39:12.617 --> 00:39:14.381
You can't charge people nothing.

00:39:14.552 --> 00:39:18.318
Stay out of this, Dr. I-Can't-Diagnose-You-
Without-an-Appointment.

00:39:18.489 --> 00:39:19.752
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:39:19.924 --> 00:39:23.326
All right. Hold on. Dr. Abbott's got a point.
I can't just charge nothing.

00:39:23.494 --> 00:39:27.260
I'll tell you what I'm gonna do. From
this moment on, I'm doubling my prices.

00:39:27.432 --> 00:39:28.866
Oh, that's funny.
He's funny.

00:39:31.736 --> 00:39:32.828
So....

00:39:33.004 --> 00:39:35.439
So it's true.
You are a part of this madness.

00:39:35.607 --> 00:39:38.201
Well, what was I supposed to do?
You got rid of me.

00:39:38.376 --> 00:39:40.868
- You quit.
- You cut back my hours.

00:39:41.045 --> 00:39:43.673
And don't give me
that bogus reason why.

00:39:43.848 --> 00:39:46.783
You know the real reason.
The whole town does.

00:39:46.951 --> 00:39:50.410
You have done some ludicrous,
asinine things in your lifetime...

00:39:50.588 --> 00:39:54.889
...but working for this man?
Oh, that takes the cake, Mother.

00:39:55.460 --> 00:39:57.690
Move it or lose it, Junior.

00:40:02.367 --> 00:40:03.698
Hey.

00:40:04.736 --> 00:40:07.728
I expected you wouldn't talk to me,
so I brought a peace offer--

00:40:07.906 --> 00:40:10.307
Why should I talk to you?
So you can lie to me more?

00:40:10.475 --> 00:40:13.240
I didn't lie to you.
I just didn't tell you the whole truth.

00:40:13.411 --> 00:40:16.176
- Do you have a boyfriend?
- Yes.

00:40:16.347 --> 00:40:18.748
I want you to meet him.
If you do, you'll understand.

00:40:18.917 --> 00:40:20.783
That was on my list
of things to do.

00:40:20.952 --> 00:40:24.354
Right between picking up my dry cleaning
and chopping off my hand.

00:40:25.757 --> 00:40:28.988
He's in Denver. That's three hours
away from here, four by bus.

00:40:29.160 --> 00:40:31.390
To make it back by dinner,
we have to leave now.

00:40:32.063 --> 00:40:33.394
You're serious about this?

00:40:34.299 --> 00:40:35.824
Come with me.

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:39.959
After that, you don't have to talk
to me ever again if you don't want to.

00:40:44.709 --> 00:40:48.009
- That's it for the patients. I'm Audi 5000.
- Hold on there a second.

00:40:48.179 --> 00:40:50.079
- You want to talk about something?
- I do.

00:40:50.248 --> 00:40:53.115
I wasn't entirely forthcoming regarding
my previous employment.

00:40:53.284 --> 00:40:54.274
Hardly.

00:40:54.452 --> 00:40:58.150
I should've told you Old Tight-ass
was my son. Apologies, Sparky.

00:40:58.323 --> 00:41:01.850
I'm happy to have you here, but if working
for me is some revenge scheme--

00:41:02.026 --> 00:41:04.324
Heck, no. I need the gig.

00:41:04.495 --> 00:41:08.625
Though I got to admit, I did enjoy the look
on that sour apple's face this morning.

00:41:08.800 --> 00:41:11.770
- You want to tell me what happened?
- His pops died two years ago.

00:41:11.936 --> 00:41:14.371
I got re-hitched not long thereafter.

00:41:14.539 --> 00:41:18.305
It caused a scandal in the community.
Junior thought it was affecting business.

00:41:18.476 --> 00:41:20.968
Not to mention he was never
crazy about the new beau.

00:41:21.145 --> 00:41:23.204
So he cut back my hours, and I quit.

00:41:23.381 --> 00:41:24.871
How soon after did you remarry?

00:41:25.049 --> 00:41:26.483
- Two months.
- Two months?

00:41:26.651 --> 00:41:28.710
Do I strike you
as the mourning type?

00:41:28.886 --> 00:41:30.251
No, not really.

00:41:30.421 --> 00:41:33.322
Anyway, I knew where Junior
was coming from.

00:41:33.491 --> 00:41:34.890
He worshipped his pops.

00:41:35.059 --> 00:41:36.390
Never got on with him.

00:41:36.561 --> 00:41:37.858
But he sure did worship him.

00:41:38.029 --> 00:41:41.192
The truth is, they were exactly alike.

00:41:41.966 --> 00:41:43.695
You think that's possible?

00:41:43.868 --> 00:41:47.668
That a father and son who don't get along
can actually have something in common?

00:41:47.839 --> 00:41:51.241
In my experience,
when a father and son don't get along...

00:41:51.409 --> 00:41:54.470
...it usually means
they got everything in common.

00:41:58.483 --> 00:42:01.942
There's my hunk of burning love
as we speak. See you on the flip side.

00:42:02.120 --> 00:42:03.747
So long, Edna.

00:42:24.742 --> 00:42:26.608
So this is your boyfriend.

00:42:28.346 --> 00:42:31.805
Ephram Brown,
meet Colin Hart.

00:42:37.388 --> 00:42:40.790
Colin grew up
down the block from me.

00:42:40.958 --> 00:42:43.017
We did everything together.

00:42:43.861 --> 00:42:46.956
He was the first boy I ever hated.

00:42:47.265 --> 00:42:49.495
The first boy I ever hit.

00:42:49.667 --> 00:42:51.396
Kissed.

00:42:52.904 --> 00:42:56.363
Bright and him were best friends.
They were always getting into trouble.

00:42:56.541 --> 00:42:59.875
And last Fourth of July, they decided
to swipe Colin's dad's truck...

00:43:00.044 --> 00:43:02.376
...and go for a joy ride.

00:43:02.547 --> 00:43:06.381
Colin drove.
There was an accident.

00:43:09.921 --> 00:43:13.118
Bright was thrown from the vehicle.
He doesn't remember what happened.

00:43:13.291 --> 00:43:16.625
By the time the ambulance got there,
Colin had fallen unconscious.

00:43:18.029 --> 00:43:20.191
He hasn't woken up ever since.

00:43:20.698 --> 00:43:25.363
Every night, I've prayed for a miracle,
but nothing happens.

00:43:25.903 --> 00:43:28.600
When I heard about your dad
coming to town, I thought:

00:43:28.773 --> 00:43:31.970
"Anyone could help him,
it would be him, right?"

00:43:35.346 --> 00:43:38.281
I'm sorry if I hurt your feelings, Ephram.

00:43:39.851 --> 00:43:42.183
I was gonna tell you,
I just....

00:43:43.621 --> 00:43:45.749
I didn't know how.

00:43:50.962 --> 00:43:53.488
- It smells good.
- Which in and of itself is a success.

00:43:53.664 --> 00:43:57.567
- What are you cooking?
- Only the finest in haute cuisine.

00:43:58.436 --> 00:44:00.632
Reheated Kentucky Fried Chicken.

00:44:00.805 --> 00:44:02.204
I'm gonna set the table.

00:44:02.373 --> 00:44:05.138
Oh, Delia, wait.
This could be my first edible meal.

00:44:05.309 --> 00:44:07.334
Go down to the basement,
get the silverware.

00:44:07.512 --> 00:44:09.742
- I'll get the fine china.
- Okay.

00:44:21.626 --> 00:44:23.958
He never even looks me
in the eyes anymore.

00:44:28.166 --> 00:44:30.260
It's because you don't talk to him.

00:44:30.768 --> 00:44:33.169
- I talk to him.
- You talk at him.

00:44:33.337 --> 00:44:36.204
Try asking him how his day was.
Try listening.

00:44:38.042 --> 00:44:39.373
Delia's so much easier.

00:44:39.544 --> 00:44:42.070
- She's 4, Andy.
- It doesn't matter.

00:44:42.246 --> 00:44:44.578
She's always known
how much I love her.

00:44:45.149 --> 00:44:49.108
Somehow I've never been able
to get that message through to him.

00:44:50.555 --> 00:44:51.852
Well, call me an optimist.

00:44:52.023 --> 00:44:55.550
But this is one case, doctor,
that's not terminal.

00:44:58.095 --> 00:44:59.790
Hey, guess what.
I figured it out.

00:44:59.964 --> 00:45:01.193
Figured what out?

00:45:01.365 --> 00:45:04.733
- Where to go if something happens to me.
- Not this macabre subject again.

00:45:04.902 --> 00:45:06.199
Everwood, Colorado.

00:45:06.370 --> 00:45:07.599
Where?

00:45:07.772 --> 00:45:09.740
When I was a kid...

00:45:09.907 --> 00:45:13.172
...I took this train trip
with my parents across the country.

00:45:13.344 --> 00:45:17.975
There was a snowstorm and we had to stop
for a day in a town called Everwood.

00:45:18.649 --> 00:45:21.346
It was the most beautiful place
I'd ever seen, Andy.

00:45:21.519 --> 00:45:24.489
It was on this hill
surrounded by the Rockies.

00:45:25.056 --> 00:45:27.354
And I remember thinking
even then:

00:45:27.825 --> 00:45:30.226
"This is what heaven
must look like."

00:45:31.729 --> 00:45:36.132
There's no chance this place is also
a major center for neurosurgery, is there?

00:45:36.300 --> 00:45:37.631
Sorry.

00:45:37.802 --> 00:45:39.429
That's the other part of the deal.

00:45:39.604 --> 00:45:42.096
No more working for the rich
and famous, doctor.

00:45:42.273 --> 00:45:44.435
Even small-town folk
need medical miracles.

00:45:44.609 --> 00:45:46.338
I'll have to start writing this down.

00:45:46.510 --> 00:45:49.536
Just remember one thing.
Everwood, Colorado.

00:45:49.914 --> 00:45:51.507
That's where I'll be.

00:45:52.016 --> 00:45:55.748
- You can't be in the Bahamas?
- Nope. Everwood or bust.

00:45:59.056 --> 00:46:01.286
Then that's where I'll be too.

00:46:12.203 --> 00:46:14.228
Listen....

00:46:14.405 --> 00:46:15.804
Delia, we should talk about this.

00:46:15.973 --> 00:46:18.465
It's okay, Dad.
I know what's wrong with you.

00:46:19.343 --> 00:46:20.606
You do?

00:46:20.778 --> 00:46:23.110
You have a distraught heart.

00:46:25.216 --> 00:46:26.684
Yeah.

00:46:27.652 --> 00:46:29.416
Yeah, I do.

00:46:29.887 --> 00:46:31.377
Come here.

00:46:37.595 --> 00:46:41.122
- I love you so much, kiddo.
- l love you too, Dad.

00:47:02.586 --> 00:47:04.452
You're playing.

00:47:05.122 --> 00:47:07.090
I felt like it, that's all.

00:47:07.725 --> 00:47:10.820
I'm gonna finish
setting the table.

00:47:27.311 --> 00:47:28.938
How was your day?

00:47:29.113 --> 00:47:30.774
It was okay.

00:47:30.948 --> 00:47:33.645
I'm in love with a girl
who's in love with a guy in a coma.

00:47:33.818 --> 00:47:35.547
Other than that, it was standard.

00:47:45.796 --> 00:47:47.787
About the other day...

00:47:48.032 --> 00:47:50.057
...I said some things I didn't mean.

00:47:50.534 --> 00:47:52.093
We both did.

00:47:54.138 --> 00:47:57.472
- And that comment about my beard?
- Well, that I meant.

00:47:58.509 --> 00:48:00.910
- I'm not shaving it, you know.
- So don't.

00:48:01.912 --> 00:48:05.473
It's ugly, but it's also
kind of distinguished.

00:48:05.983 --> 00:48:08.645
Distinguished?
Why do you say that?

00:48:09.053 --> 00:48:10.282
I don't know.

00:48:10.454 --> 00:48:12.081
It just is.

00:48:15.926 --> 00:48:17.894
You play so well.

00:48:19.063 --> 00:48:20.792
I'd forgotten how good you are.

00:48:22.233 --> 00:48:24.463
Mom used to say
I had your hands.

00:48:37.848 --> 00:48:41.011
And there they sat,
father and son...

00:48:41.919 --> 00:48:45.253
...like they were sitting
together for the first time.

00:48:46.957 --> 00:48:52.020
No, I wasn't there the day
Dr. Brown's life changed forever.

00:48:53.230 --> 00:48:56.222
But I was around
for many days thereafter...

00:48:56.400 --> 00:48:58.232
...when he and his family...

00:48:58.402 --> 00:49:00.461
...would call Everwood...

00:49:00.638 --> 00:49:02.072
...their home.

00:49:45.082 --> 00:49:47.073
[ENGLISH]
